wiki/compile.md:35:- **No recursive schemas.** A schema whose subtree contains a cycle throws `ZodCompileUnsupportedError` and parses through the runtime. Input containing a reference cycle terminates because the memoizer registers each in-progress output before its children run, keyed on the parse context every schema in that call shares; a generated fast path takes an input and returns a value, so it has no context to key on and would follow the cycle until the stack ran out. A compiled node also hands back to the runtime when the value it receives is a memoizer back edge, so a transform sitting on a cycle still raises `$ZodCyclicError` from its own parse. Supporting this properly means threading the parse context and `memo.alloc` into generated containers.
